# Bot2's Pest Infestation (X = 1) makes two Pest tokens ("when this token dies, you gain 1 life") and is exiled with a void
# counter as it resolves, being a card. On turn 7 Bot1's Infernal Grasp destroys a Pest: a token is not a card (CR 108.2), so
# Dauthi Voidwalker does not replace it - it goes to the graveyard, dies, and Bot2 gains the life.
# (The Haywire Mite scenario is the positive control: a creature card never dies there.)

